# AI Collaboration Checklist

Load with any substantial task (complements `chinese-listener-core.mdc`).

## Before coding

- [ ] If user used `@docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md`, read **full docs bundle** per `chinese-listener-docs-bundle.mdc`; otherwise read `docs/WHAT_WE_DO.md` + relevant docs. Always read `.cursor/rules/chinese-listener-architecture.mdc` for layer placement and power impact
- [ ] Searched repo for existing patterns under `app/src/main`
- [ ] Identified **affected packages** and **layer** (ui/presentation/domain/data)
- [ ] Stated root cause or investigation gaps
- [ ] Proposed plan; **user approved** (unless explicit skip)
- [ ] Named verification: Gradle task + unit tests if logic changed + device/emulator if UI/Android
- [ ] New/changed Kotlin follows `chinese-listener-code-style.mdc` (collections, no `for`/`while`; refactor batches use REFACTOR_GUIDE)

## During implementation

- [ ] Minimal diff; match existing package `com.example.chineselistener`; new code in correct subpackage (`ui`, `presentation`, `domain`, `data`, `theme`)
- [ ] No new dependencies without approval and Gradle file update
- [ ] No repository/network/DB calls from composables; no `GlobalScope`; no unapproved polling/wake locks (see `chinese-listener-energy-efficiency.mdc`)
- [ ] `minSdk` / permissions unchanged unless in scope

## After implementation

- [ ] Ran verification or reported blockers
- [ ] Summarized changes with `startLine:endLine:path` citations
- [ ] Git read-only unless user asked for commits; **never push**

## Plan quality

Include behavior path (UI event → state → side effects), **energy impact** (foreground/background, cancellation), conventions used (with file refs), and regression check — not only a file list.
